implementationPlan.description:
Verification, run once at the end. Run checkRef GREEN exactly as written, from the worktree root. It does the following:
- archives HEAD's packages/moe-daemon to /tmp;
- overlays index.ts, server/probeHost.ts, commands/doctor.ts and commands/doctor.bindHost.test.ts from the checkout;
- runs npm ci, tsc on the package, and tsc with a temporary tsconfig for the new test file;
- runs vitest verbose on doctor.test.ts, doctor.bindHost.test.ts and index.test.ts.
It requires vitest to exit 0 and 'B rows passed: 9/9'. Never run npm in the shared checkout (project rail).
Then run checkRef UNCHANGED: doctor.test.ts must be byte-identical to 6d6bdc51 (DoD 3). Submit GREEN's command, exitCode and output tail as the complete_task verification. The architect's dry run printed 'Test Files 3 passed (3)', 'Tests 147 passed | 1 skipped (148)' and 'B rows passed: 9/9', in about 15 s.
Error handling for a red run: the gate prints the ../v.log tail. Fix the code; never weaken, skip or rename a row. A ::1 skip shows 6/9 and fails on purpose. See mem:gotcha-daemon-subprocess-tests for counting verbose check lines and for running tsc on a test file.
